config DRM
    tristate "DRM/KMS for the VMware SVGA framebuffer"
    default y
    help
      Linux DRM and vmwgfx userspace interfaces for the VMware SVGA II
      function already bound by the boot framebuffer. Selecting M builds
      drm.ko. Device discovery and publication occur when the module loads;
      the early framebuffer and console remain permanent kernel services.
      Open card/PRIME descriptors, mappings, asynchronous jobs, resources and
      hardware callbacks retain the exact module until safely retired.
